    'Fraction of the total variance due to differences between subjects (and not to raters or error): the reliability of a repeated measurement. There are six forms of Shrout and Fleiss and ten of McGraw and Wong, by model (one-way, two-way random or mixed), type (consistency or absolute agreement) and unit (single or average).',
